content.text:
Would it work to use the following: a v_\parallel flux (\hat{G}) like

\hat{G} = {\dot{v} * f} - s(\dot{v}) * [\dot{v} * f]

where \dot{v} is the advecting scalar in the v_parallel direction (acceleration) and 

s(\dot{v}) = \begin{cases}
sign([\dot{v}]) \quad |{\dot{v}}| > 0.01 * \max(|\dot{v}_L|,|\dot{v}_R|) \\
0 \quad \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}

?

Before testing the Rusanov flux, can you create a plan for implementing the closer version of what I proposed, that you suggested?  i mean

  [
  s(a)=
  \begin{cases}
  \operatorname{sign}({a}),&
  |{a}|>\epsilon\max(|a_L|,|a_R|),\
  0,&\text{otherwise}.
  \end{cases}
  ]

Make a plan to edit the Maxima that generates the kernels and gk_collisionless_flux.

